x.c('execution_binding',0,19,29,'Execution-scoped binding','Binding joins concrete Worker to required GTL Role before realization and records admitted program/digest, immutable WorkspaceBinding/digest, published GraphFunction membership, optional durable Job, run, worker, role, execution basis and invocation authority.')
x.q('program_binding_admission',0,19,33,'execution_binding','Public semantic work enters through one admitted overlay/program composition and one published member GraphFunction, with Job when durable semantic identity is declared. Job/function/overlay row/bare vector cannot replace the whole program or be used outside membership. Validate against exact program, workspace, function membership, resolved policy and invocation authority before execution/approval. Module.graphs exposes all live internal vectors before public carrier traversal; every reachable live vector publishes a lawful RefinementBoundary or CandidateFamily, otherwise fail closed.')
x.q('leaf_realization_binding',0,25,29,'execution_binding','When HoG traverses a published GraphFunction with an implementation realizing leaf effects, preserve program, exact selected-action/current-intent basis, function/membership, workspace, graph-call, execution-basis, implementation and materialization identities. Authentication/authority resolution remain external; ABG records their resolved inputs.',conditions=['Published GraphFunction traversal realizes declared leaf effects.'])
x.c('runtime_environment',0,35,45,'Traversal runtime environment','Each executable boundary resolves a snapshot from live vector contract and any published function environment, distinguishing external entry from internally produced carried bindings.')
x.q('required_carried_boundary',0,37,45,'runtime_environment execution_binding','Fail closed on conflicting carried contracts and do not dispatch proof/production without required internally produced bindings. Target asset_surface.required_contexts belongs to the executable boundary and must exist in the published carrier environment. Preserve target/environment asset kind, required contexts and standards/output refs in prompts/manifests. Any merge widening a live vector is explicit and invocation-local, never rewrites module topology; separately retain vector-source, asset-required and effective required bindings in prompts, manifests and events.')
x.c('workspace_authority_binding',0,47,61,'Stable workspace authority and immutable binding','WorkspaceAuthorityBasis contains only stable identity, canonical root, authority mode and authority-bearing manifest/config truth; immutable WorkspaceBinding adds exact installed product set, resolved lock and declared roots. Mutable observations, readiness, projection, replay cursors and root content are not authority identity.')
x.q('distinct_workspaces_and_observation',0,47,51,'workspace_authority_binding','Distinct input/output workspace authority must be admitted with both stable bases and immutable bindings; derive output assets/materialization under output root and preserve both lineages in handoff/events/projection. Every re-observation of file/process/runtime/replay/readiness/worksite truth creates or admits a new ObservationSnapshot on the same binding if authority is unchanged; it may stale dependent model/gap/next-action projections but neither mutates binding nor causes basis_fork_detected.',conditions=['Distinct workspaces are declared or mutable truth is re-observed.'])
x.q('binding_basis_crossing',0,53,61,'workspace_authority_binding execution_binding','Changed authority, installed products, lock or root requires separate admitted immutable binding. Catalog/view change may require a new execution basis and declaration reprice but not a new binding unless a constituent changed. Crossing an execution basis or binding on an existing causal spine needs exact covering declaration reprice naming the crossed pair; absent this return typed basis_fork_detected before execution.')
x.q('stdo_environment_admission',0,63,77,'execution_binding','For a Program declaring an STDO environment, validate/admit exact released native-source binding, required material, permitted acquisition and each explicitly selected supplementary representation/index/corpus implementation with source relationship. Establish all required context/access evidence and permission before dependent work. Native access neither adds unselected companions nor bypasses declared content, permission, identity, completeness or access checks. Locators are resource assertions, not authority/release proof; missing/ambiguous/mismatched/inaccessible/unpermitted required inputs produce typed refusal/block before dispatch. Caller retrieval and successful tool exit alone do not establish binding; access checks neither apply STDO meaning, choose work nor accept semantics.',conditions=['The Program declares an STDO environment.'])
x.u('binding_external_contracts',0,63,77,'execution_binding','This criteria section references GTL, workspace, environment and reprice contracts whose full definitions and cross-chunk identities are not supplied.','The binding obligations and fail-closed boundaries are retained without constructing those external identities.')
x.disposition(0,'residual','Binding laws retained; referenced contracts remain local names without cross-chunk resolution.')
x.c('c_call_envelope',1,9,18,'Uniform compute call envelope','C means compute: one instantiation of a tuple over F_D, F_P, F_H at one program stage. The admitted GTL C declaration supplies the structure; the declared shape is data and the handler realizes compute. Fibre is data inside one uniform truth envelope, not surrounding structure.')
x.u('c_call_metadata_authority',1,3,7,'c_call_envelope','The source labels T-283 F_H closure and cites T-200, T-287 and other derivations; their evidence is not supplied.','Treat accepted status and lineage as source metadata, not independently established current acceptance.')
x.disposition(1,'residual','Compute ontology retained; claimed historical acceptance and referenced derivation are not independently verified.')
x.c('c_call_spine',2,22,58,'Compute call event spine','Every invoking stage-task has exactly one ordered opened → fibre_selected → evidenced(0..n) → result_admitted → judged spine, with no arm/fibre/role/plugin exemption; a composed batch is a grouping ref, not the counted call. Opened records locus only. Fibre dispatch/invocation/payload/response/execution/escalation events exist only within an open spine through evidenced references.')
x.q('spine_identity_and_selection',2,26,51,'c_call_spine','Opened locus includes cCallRef,basisId,graphFunctionId,graphCallId,frameId,edge,vectorIndex,stageRole,taskOrdinal|null,attempt. Spine locus carries neither fibre nor fibre-dependent instruction material. fibre_selected is the first interior row, with cCallRef/regime/armId/compositionRef|null resolved from admitted role×fibre and implementations at one seam. cCallRef is an injective stable typed-tuple digest, never collision-prone delimiter joining. Open-program calls also include programLocusRef and possibly empty positive-integer retryPath together in locus and digest; recursive frames, repeated calls, tasks, serial same-role loci and nested attempts cannot collapse. All 5.0 standard calls carry both; flat compatibility is not release-authoritative.')
x.c('c_call_judgment',2,63,84,'Compute call judgment','Judgment is advance/retry/pending/blocked/escalated/no_declared_check. pending is fibre-independent external waiting, projected publicly as dispatch_required. One retryable-failure allowlist governs outcomes across arms; selection-row single-event guards anchor dispatch temporal properties, non-vacuous on every executed arm.')
x.q('no_check_and_replay_audit',2,63,84,'c_call_judgment c_call_spine','no_declared_check never satisfies a gate or declared required check; it advances only when no check is demanded. Pre-envelope replay derives a spine at read time without synthetic truth events. For every completed run, archived external work sessions equal external-work-bearing replay spine invocations per F_P/external F_H arm; F_D supplies deterministic evidence artifacts instead. The standing gate measures both.')
x.v('fibre_substitution_invariance',2,59,62,'c_call_spine',allowed=['Substitute fibre selection payload and evidence class; all-F_D realizes workflow and all-F_H a human process.'],forbidden=['Change spine kinds, order, count or replay shape with fibre choice.'])
x.c('declared_child_traversal',2,86,94,'Declared child traversal placement','A call may resolve as child traversal with sub_traversal evidence and child basis/run refs. Atomic session versus transparent sub-traversal is declared per call; the same spine law holds recursively and each boundary reconciles its own archives/invocations using collision-free graphCall/frame identity.')
x.r('recursive_call_enclosure',2,86,94,'declared_child_traversal','c_call_spine','obeys','A declared child traversal retains the uniform spine and audit equality at its own boundary.',True)
x.q('open_program_role_authority',2,96,109,'c_call_envelope c_call_spine','The C algebra is an admitted open composition, not a fixed triple. A library may declare transform/evaluate/consequence but there is no hidden default. Every program names its result-bearing role whose admitted payload feeds closure/carry and uses the same router/retry law. Spine accepts nonempty roles; validation/admission enforces program membership and out-of-program roles are drift. Preparation, result-admission and materialization bind rows are mechanics, never stages or satisfaction of stage count, result-bearing role, order or substitution law.')
x.v('cognitive_compression',2,111,117,'c_call_envelope',allowed=['By declaration and replay-assessed worker capability, make plan/critique/repair-guidance explicit stages or inline instruction categories.'],forbidden=['Inline verification: F_D admission, deterministic execution and evaluate judgment remain explicit trust-boundary stages.','Use self-declared capability instead of replay assessment.'])
x.q('named_program_and_adaptation',2,119,132,'c_call_envelope','Programs and functions are named GTL declarations published through Module/catalog and traversed directly by HoG. abg.hog_program/catalog/ref, generated handler programs and interpreter-local config cannot replace/select them. Retry/escalation/branching/alternative compute requires admitted graph/C structure with explicit predicates, policies, bounds and terminal cases; HoG evaluates it against admitted replay facts and ABG records selected locus/regime/implementation/judgment/continuation. Private ladders, adapter selectors, hidden fallback and generated programs are prohibited.')
x.q('current_input_conservation',2,134,142,'c_call_envelope','Each call consumes input at its actual traversal position. Sequential composition preserves admitted producer-consumer transfer and declared transformation under existing basis. Admission/recovery cannot replace progressed value with graph-entry input or infer provenance from payload equality. Nested entry/foldback preserve declared causal relations. Proof fixtures must exercise actual relationships with successor different from entry, not invent a new basis.')
x.u('c_call_operational_projection_limit',2,22,142,'c_call_spine','Event ordering, digest injectivity, replay audits and temporal laws are specified obligations; no execution or proof is performed by this representation.','Implementation conformity and operational verification remain unresolved.')
